WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.067
In pretrial hearings

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.634
today, the judge

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.103
overseeing the $1.6 billion

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.904
defamation lawsuit brought by Dominion

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:05.672
voting systems

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.272
against Fox

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.207
tore into the network

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.476
today, saying he was concerned, quote,

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.111
there have been misrepresentations

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:11.878
to the court

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.079
day after saying Fox

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.048
had a, quote, credibility problem.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.716
Both comments were about Rupert Murdoch's

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.650
role in the network.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.918
The judge said he plans to appoint

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.919
an outside attorney

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.321
called a special master

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.856
to investigate whether Fox lied

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.923
and withheld key evidence.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:24.724
Dominion argues

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.660
that Fox narrowly defined Murdoch's role,

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.429
limiting what Fox turned over

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.230
during Discovery.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.264
Now, it happened a day

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.632
before jury selection begins

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.299
and after a series

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.267
of damaging revelations

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.402
about the network.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:38.304
Randi Kaye has that part of the story.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.573
The outcome of our presidential election

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.275
was seized from the hands of voters.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:42.976
Fox News

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:43.610
host Tucker

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.711
Carlson backing

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.880
former President Donald Trump on air.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.314
But private text messages

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.883
sent by Carlson released

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.817
as part of the Dominion

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.052
Voting Systems lawsuit

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.753
against Fox News show

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.089
how he really feels about Trump.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.791
According to the messages, Carlson

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:58.658
actually hates

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.993
Trump passionately

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.328
and views his presidency as a disaster.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.097
Two days before the Capitol

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.732
insurrection, Carlson wrote,

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.167
We are very, very close

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.701
to being able to ignore Trump.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.071
Most nights, I truly can't wait.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.139
On January six, Carlson

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.175
texted his producer calling Trump

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.344
a demonic force, a destroyer Carlson

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.413
described Trump's post-election behavior

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.915
as disgusting.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.283
Is the fix already in?

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.818
It wasn't just Carlson.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.020
Other Fox hosts who repeatedly featured

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.055
Trump's election fraud claims on air.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.024
Nobody like Dominion voting systems

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.592
were also mocking Trump

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.828
and his lawyers behind the scenes.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.496
Court documents reveal Fox

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.064
anchors and executives

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:38.765
used words

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.866
like ludicrous

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.869
mind blowingly nuts and totally insane.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.737
Carlson texted other hosts,

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.172
including Laura Ingraham,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.241
about Trump lawyer Sidney Powell,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.343
saying, Powell is lying, by the way,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.277
I called her.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.580
It's insane, Ingraham responded.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.348
Sidney is a complete nut.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.950
No one will work with her.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.785
Court documents released in the case

00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.953
also include an email

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.921
from Fox Chairman Rupert Murdoch

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.889
describing Trump's

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.658
election lies as bull and damaging.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.061
In Murdoch's January deposition,

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:08.862
he conceded

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.830
that some Fox hosts were endorsing

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.632
Trump's falsehoods about the 2020

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.100
election being stolen.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.135
Murdoch said,

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.736
I would have liked us to be stronger

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.872
in denouncing it in hindsight.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.039
Murdoch's deposition

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:20.940
also reveals

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.741
that he rejected

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:22.842
his own network's

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.011
conspiracy theories about Dominion.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.880
When asked by Dominion's lawyers,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.081
Do you believe that Dominion

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:28.681
was engaged

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.349
in a massive

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.651
and coordinated effort to steal the 2020

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.086
presidential election?

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.321
Murdoch replied, No.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.756
Promotion of the false claims

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.758
was also rejected by the network's

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.260
DC managing editor.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.895
Court documents show.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.430
In my 22 years affiliated with Fox,

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.899
this is the closest thing

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.001
I've seen to an existential crisis,

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.802
at least journalistically.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.804
Bill Sammon wrote to a colleague.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.506
Still, Fox News denies

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.175
wrongdoing and says it was reporting

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.643
on newsworthy allegations

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.011
about the election

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.312
Why were Fox hosts

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.547
saying one thing on the air

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.282
and something else privately?

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.416
Dominion contends

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.851
this was all about business

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.519
and not alienating the base

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.887
loyal to Trump.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.055
When Fox reporters

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.523
tried to report the facts,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.824
they were attacked.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:12.659
Court filings

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.259
show Tucker

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.661
Carlson was livid

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.796
after a Fox News reporter Fact-Check

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.598
Trump's tweet about votes

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.400
allegedly being destroyed.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.168
Carlson texted coworkers.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.403
Please get her fired.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.104
Seriously, what the F.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.739
It needs to stop immediately.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:27.707
Like tonight,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.542
it's measurably hurting the company.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.044
The stock price is down.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.212
Not a joke.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.313
Documents from court

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.013
also show

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:34.614
Fox News

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.583
Chief Suzanne Scott was furious

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:37.617
after a correspondent

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:38.551
for the network fact

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.086
checked Trump's election lies,

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.355
warning it was bad for business.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.556
In this email, Scott

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.358
said this has to stop now.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.960
The audience is furious

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.127
and we are just feeding them

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.296
material bad for business.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.364
In another revealing

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.665
email, Murdoch explained

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.366
why Hannity

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.602
continued to promote election lies,

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.436
saying Hannity

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.104
had been privately disgusted

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.472
by Trump for weeks

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.674
but was scared to lose viewers.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.010
Randi Kaye joins us now.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.278
What stands out to you

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.045
in the details

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:06.546
that have emerged

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.182
in court filings by Dominion

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.584
Well, Anderson, what's remarkable

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.785
in these legal filings is

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.920
you can see how worried

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.822
Fox hosts and executives were.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.156
They were worried about losing business.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:17.790
They were also worried

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.725
about losing viewers,

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.059
certainly to Newsmax,

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.027
which was also pushing

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.363
these false election conspiracy theories.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.697
And when you look at the whole breadth

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.633
of the text messages in the emails,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.868
you can really see the Fox business model

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.770
at least according to Dominion.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.471
They have said that

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.172
it's not about delivering the truth.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:33.873
Dominion says

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.275
that it's about pushing content

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.377
and conspiracy theories to these viewers,

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.244
feeding them

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.979
all of that to keep them hooked.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.114
Now, more specifically,

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.082
Dominion has alleged in the lawsuit

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.450
that Fox News recklessly

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.718
disregarded the truth

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:46.986
because it was more concerned

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:47.920
about business

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.188
and Dominion is now saying

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.857
that these emails, text messages

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.892
and also the deposition testimony

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.527
speak for themselves Anderson.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.461
Randi Kaye, appreciate it.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:55.962
Thank you.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:56.562
Perspective now

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.063
from retired

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.831
First Amendment lawyer Leigh Levine

00:04:58.831 --> 00:04:59.399
was represented

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.333
on Fox News, CNN

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.167
and many other media

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.669
organizations in his distinguished

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.570
40 years of practice.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:04.804
Leigh,

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:05.672
when you hear the developments

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:05.938
in court

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.506
today, the judge

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.674
accusing Fox, his legal team

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:08.975
making misrepresentations,

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:09.876
saying he's likely to appoint

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.011
a special master to investigate.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:12.779
Is that a big deal

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.813
to run afoul of the judge

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.548
like this on the eve of the trial?

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.950
Oh, yes, it is a very big deal, Anderson.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.186
It's a big deal on three levels.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:20.620
First,

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.422
one of the things that the judge said

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:23.423
today

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:24.090
was that

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.292
he was likely going to give the jury

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.660
what's called an adverse

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.462
inference instruction,

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.730
which means that he's

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.332
going to tell them that

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:36.302
because Fox did not produce

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.971
information in discovery

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.007
that hampered Dominion

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.009
in its ability to defend the case,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.713
the jury can infer from that

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:47.780
that the information

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.716
that Fox didn't provide

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:52.085
would have been helpful to Dominion.

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:54.287
And that is coming from the judge

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.456
that will be very powerful to the jury,

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:59.158
especially on top of all of the emails

00:05:59.158 --> 00:05:59.892
and texts

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:02.228
that you just discussed on the air.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.997
The judge, Judge Davis, also sanctioned

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:05.598
Fox, basically

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:06.866
saying Dominion can conduct

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.768
new depositions with witnesses.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.136
And if they do, Fox

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.604
has to pick up the costs.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:12.138
I don't know

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:12.839
if Dominion

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.707
will actually take the judge up on that

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:15.475
on the offer,

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:16.576
if there will be other sanctions,

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:17.610
if you were

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:17.810
I mean,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.112
if you were representing Dominion,

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.380
how would you want to proceed?

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.582
Is would new depositions mean

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:23.583
a halt to the trial?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.986
Not necessarily.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:27.720
There are

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.721
obviously going to be

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:31.057
a number of witnesses in the case,

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:33.526
the ones that are impacted

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.294
by the new information

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.662
that has just recently

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:39.866
been turned over by Fox to Dominion

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.002
are very few.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.771
So theoretically,

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:47.340
those depositions could be taking place

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.775
at another location

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:50.910
while the trial is going on.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.147
And Fox could make those witnesses

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:56.115
available both for the depositions

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:58.050
and then for their trial testimony.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.751
And Dominion

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.253
could have the

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:02.522
advantage of having that information

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.923
gleaned from the deposition

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:04.757
when they actually put

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.225
the witnesses on the stand.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.760
And this revelation is Rupert

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.328
Murdoch apparently held dual roles

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.430
at both Fox News,

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.632
as well as his parent company, Fox Corp..

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.101
Could that explain why that has.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:15.301
I mean,

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.569
why does that have the potential

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:17.370
to be significant to

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.404
this case is just that

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.706
they didn't specify that to Dominion.

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.075
That's what Dominion is claiming.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:23.810
Dominion.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.411
And the judge as well

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.246
seems to be of the view

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.816
that that question about Rupert Murdoch's

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:31.984
role at Fox News,

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:34.420
whether he was, in fact, an officer of

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.221
the company

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:39.392
Fox misstated

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:42.795
or did not disclose that he was.

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:45.865
And now it has belatedly disclosed

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.266
that he was.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:50.136
And the judge is very concerned

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:52.839
that that was a misrepresentation

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:54.841
that prejudiced Dominion

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.809
because it if it had known

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.578
if Dominion had known

00:07:58.578 --> 00:07:59.545
that Murdoch

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.647
was an officer of the corporation,

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:02.515
it would have

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:06.052
arguably be entitled to a broader

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.287
array of documents

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.156
to be produced from Murdoch,

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:12.158
because he would have had

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:12.625
at least

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.393
theoretically, control

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.429
over a broader range of documents.

00:08:16.596 --> 00:08:18.297
And they never got those documents.

